      <h3>Step 3: The Cross-Grid Domino Effect</h3>
      <p>When you accumulate enough <strong>X</strong>s in a single row or column, only one empty cell remains. That cell MUST be a confirmed match (<strong>✓</strong>). The moment you place a <strong>✓</strong>, a powerful chain reaction occurs. Because each element is unique, you can instantly fill the rest of that row and column with <strong>X</strong>s. Furthermore, any known attributes of that suspect immediately transfer to their newly matched weapon, location, or time slot.</p>

      <h2>From Accessible Warm-ups to Mind-Bending Ciphers</h2>
      <p>Progression in <em>The 10-Minute Detective</em> is built on a carefully designed difficulty curve. Cases 1 through 5 gently introduce you to single-line deductions. You'll examine trace fibers from torn silk garments in <strong>The Crimson Thread</strong> (Case #2) or decode fresh quills from writing desks in <strong>The Message in Code</strong> (Case #3).</p>

      <p>However, by the time you reach Cases 11 through 15, the training wheels are stripped away. You'll encounter:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cryptographic Evidence:</strong> Deciphering modified Vigenère keys stamped onto folded notes.</li>
        <li><strong>Acoustic & Geolocation Traces:</strong> Analyzing 900 MHz burst signals sent from pantries and matching audio waveform footsteps in north alcoves.</li>
        <li><strong>Complex Timeline Syllogisms:</strong> Where clue A references time, clue B references location, and clue C forces you to infer weapon displacement through elimination alone.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why True Crime Puzzles Are Good for Your Brain</h2>
      <p>Modern digital life bombards us with fragmented, hyper-short information bursts. Logic grid puzzles act as a mental palate cleanser. They force cognitive focus, strengthen working memory, improve categorical reasoning, and boost executive function. Beyond the cognitive benefits, there is an innate human thrill in playing the detective—putting on the hat, examining the evidence tags, and proving guilt beyond a shadow of a doubt.</p>
